	('70a69d3f-c35b-4660-b2dd-874f53ea46e3', 'lang-ja', NULL, NULL, 'gp-no-possessive', NULL, NULL, 'historical-grammar', 'の originates from Proto-Japonic *nə and was used in Old Japanese to link one noun modifying another.', 'The job has not changed in twelve hundred years: put の between two nouns and the first modifies the second. Old Japanese had other particles that did the same work (が among them, which is why 我が国 still reads as "my country"), and の is the one that stayed general.', '{}', 'Old Japanese', 'well-supported', false, true, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'claude', 1, 'claude-haiku-4-5', 'etymology-word-v1', '7aac2324-c1bd-45c0-98d4-a41e4fe19fa1', 'e765d564-330e-445c-a492-bca1a0813762', '2026-08-26 10:32:02.233', NULL, '2026-08-26 10:32:02.233', '2026-08-26 06:50:16.199796', '2026-09-04 17:15:58.754192'),
