	('e98ddea1-da36-4e8c-bad4-10dabf3fbba7', 'lang-ja', NULL, '6f5011e7-e6d7-482d-9730-7d67a4c3399a', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'rendaku', '手袋 shows rendaku: 袋 is normally ふくろ, and voices to ぶくろ as the second half of a compound.', 'ふくろ already begins a word cleanly, so nothing blocks the change. Lyman''s Law says rendaku is blocked when the second element already contains a voiced sound; ふくろ does not, so it voices. Once you can spot that, readings like てぶくろ stop needing to be memorised one at a time.', '{}', NULL, 'well-supported', false, false, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'system', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'e765d564-330e-445c-a492-bca1a0813762', '2026-08-26 10:32:36.501', NULL, '2026-08-26 10:32:36.501', '2026-08-26 10:15:15.659426', '2026-08-26 10:32:36.501'),
	('e9fd618b-f801-4a9f-b004-a914652d7a78', 'lang-ja', NULL, 'b744c236-257c-4f32-a468-640332f86a51', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'word-origin', 'It combines the te-form of the copula で with the particle も (even; too).', 'When it follows a noun, で is the te-form of the copula, and も adds the inclusive or contrastive meaning. This shows how でも can mean both "but even" when used for contrast and "even if" when used with certain verb forms.', '{}', NULL, 'well-supported', false, true, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'claude', 1, 'claude-haiku-4-5', 'etymology-word-v1', 'c4b6594a-86e7-4be4-ba05-199f2ddd4721', 'e765d564-330e-445c-a492-bca1a0813762', '2026-08-26 10:32:02.195', NULL, '2026-08-26 10:32:02.195', '2026-08-26 06:41:07.239436', '2026-08-26 10:32:02.195'),
